        "id": 16
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-06T22:20:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem right.\n\nWhat\u0027s the purpose for that service account ?\nRight now we currently have one service account that spans different projects.\n\nSo we have a service account in default which has the role \"system:image-builder\" on the \"master\" and \"pike\" projects.\n\nYou probably want something like:\nuser: \"system:serviceaccount:default:dci.service\"\nresource_kind: role\nresource_name: \"system:image-builder\"\nnamespace: rhosp12\n\nCareful to use \":\" without double quotes, it confuses yaml.\nAlso, cluster-roles are global permissions, we\u0027re only handing out namespaced roles.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "d4977cafd3698bc802959d2216fd361c0bbf3c4b",
      "serverId": "270e2033-b340-4cff-9539-693957ebf0e7",
      "unresolved": false
    },
